# Copy to .env and fill in.  cp .env.example .env
#
# .env must EXIST as a file: scripts/slack.sh passes --env-file=.env to Node, so
# exported shell variables alone are not enough. It is gitignored; .env.example is not.
# See docs/slack-setup.md for how to create the Slack app and read these off it.

# ── Slack bridge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bot User OAuth Token. REQUIRED. Starts with "xoxb-".
# Slack app -> OAuth & Permissions -> Install to Workspace -> copy.
# Re-copy after any manifest change; reinstalling can change it.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# App-level token for Socket Mode. REQUIRED for `slack:start`. Starts with "xapp-".
# Slack app -> Basic Information -> App-Level Tokens -> Generate Token and Scopes,
# with the `connections:write` scope. This is NOT the bot token.
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=

# Optional channel allow-list. Default: empty = answer in every channel the bot is in.
# Comma-separated channel IDs (C…/G…), never names — "#brain-test" matches nothing.
# Never applied to DMs; those always work.
# SLACK_CHANNELS=C0123456789,C0987654321

# ── Runtime tuning (Slack bridge only) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Leave commented unless setting a real number: both are parsed with a bare Number(),
# so an empty value becomes 0 (every turn queues forever) and a typo becomes NaN
# (nothing is ever reaped).

# Thread sandboxes running a turn at once. Default 4.
# Each container is capped at 2g, so 4 implies an 8 GB ceiling.
# BRAIN_MAX_CONCURRENT=4

# Minutes of thread idleness before its container is removed. The volume is kept,
# so a follow-up still resumes the conversation. Default 15.
# BRAIN_IDLE_REAP_MINUTES=15

# ── Connector secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any field named in a connector's "fromEnv" map in brain.config.json is read from
# here. A connector whose variable is unset is SKIPPED SILENTLY, so check
# `bun run brain doctor` after adding one.
# The shipped github connector uses auth_type=public and needs nothing.
#
# Twenty CRM, for example:
# TWENTY_API_KEY=
